<rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:content="http://purl.org/rss/1.0/modules/content/" version="2.0"><channel><title>Personal Combined Feed</title><link>https://example.invalid</link><description>Personal aggregate feed</description><docs>http://www.rssboard.org/rss-specification</docs><generator>python-feedgen</generator><language>en</language><lastBuildDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 16:31:44 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Ask HN: If you dislike AI, why don't you prove it?</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49401293</link><description>&lt;p&gt;I've seen so many people who absolutely hate AI, and want AI companies to fail, but then 2 seconds later, open up the coding tool made by frontier labs and willingly hand them money.&lt;p&gt;Just recently convinced one of them to move away from the frontier lab lock-in to OpenCode and switch between models. Why don't more people do this?&lt;p&gt;So many people say they don't want AI to cause job loss and then the next second willingly hand over all data and money to those exact AI companies.&lt;p&gt;To be clear, I like AI, and use it all the time, but I use it in a way that allows me to easily switch models and not get locked-in.&lt;/p&gt;
